-- Suspect module for Serenity. ROUGH DRAFT / PROTOTYPE, built from an actual client-side
-- dump of the place file (Potassium/Dex export), not guesswork -- but two gaps in that dump
-- mean two things here are still best-effort:
--   - The kill weapon's own client script (whatever Tool the killer role gets) wasn't
--     present in the dump -- a client-side dump only ever captures what's actually loaded
--     for whoever's playing, and the weapon Tool only exists in a killer's Backpack once
--     the round actually assigns that role. WeaponEvent (the RemoteEvent it almost
--     certainly fires) IS confirmed to exist, but its real argument signature and the
--     server's actual attack cooldown aren't visible from this dump -- Auto Kill below
--     fires it parameterless (same convention QOD's PlayerTouchedOrClicked uses) on an
--     adjustable delay (AttackDelayBox) instead of a hardcoded guessed number, specifically
--     so the "it's slow, might be timed wrong" issue from QOD can actually be tuned live
--     against Suspect's real cooldown instead of guessed at.
--   - The ~30s can't-report-immediately window has no dedicated value anywhere in the dump
--     (no RoundTime/Intermission/GameState). Player:GetAttribute("InGame") IS confirmed
--     real (TaskFrame's own script branches on it) and flips true right as a round starts,
--     so that attribute's own change is used as the round-start clock instead of a made-up
--     timestamp.
-- Everything else (Auto Task's three minigames, Auto Report's prompt) is built directly
-- from TaskHandler/TaskLocal/TaskFrame's decompiled source and the actual ProximityPrompt
-- instances in the dump, not invented.
