-- Tunable settle delay between teleporting to a task and actually firing its prompt --
-- triggering the instant the teleport lands is the likely cause of a task's prompt/outline
-- clearing (proof the trigger DID register) while the actual minigame GUI never opens: the
-- server probably validates you've genuinely been in proximity for a moment, not just
-- teleported in and immediately interacted, and rejects it as suspicious. Live-tunable
-- since there's no way to know the real required window without testing it in Suspect
-- itself.
